# Commands Reference (Per App)

## Package Manager
- **ALL apps use Bun** -- NEVER use `npm`, `npx`, `yarn`, or `pnpm`
- Root workspace: `bun install` (installs all apps)
- Single app: `cd apps/{app}` then `bun install`

## Dev Servers

| App | Command | Port | Working Directory |
|-----|---------|------|-------------------|
| Backend | `bun run dev` | 3000 | `apps/backend` |
| Superadmin | `bun run dev` | 5173 | `apps/superadmin` |
| Company | `bun run dev` | 5174 | `apps/company` |
| Admin | `bun run dev` | 5175 | `apps/admin` |
| Conseiller | `bun run dev` | 5176 | `apps/consillier` |
| All at once | `bun run dev` | -- | Workspace root |

## Type Checking (run before every commit)

| App | Command | What it runs |
|-----|---------|-------------|
| Backend | `bun run typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` |
| Superadmin | `bun run typecheck` | `tsc -b` |
| Company | `bun run typecheck` | `tsc -b` |
| Admin | `bun run typecheck` | `tsc -b` |
| Conseiller | `bun run typecheck` | `tsc -b` |

**ALWAYS** use `bun run typecheck` -- never `npx tsc`, never `tsc` directly.

## Build

| App | Command |
|-----|---------|
| Backend | `bun run build` (runs `node build.mjs`) |
| Frontend apps | `bun run build` (runs `tsc -b && vite build`) |
| All at once | `bun run build` from workspace root |

## Linting & Formatting (Frontend apps only)

```bash
bun run lint          # ESLint
bun run format        # Prettier write
bun run format:check  # Prettier check
```

## Installing Dependencies

```bash
# Add a dependency to a specific app
cd apps/backend
bun add package-name

# Add a dev dependency
bun add -d package-name

# Install all workspace dependencies from root
bun install
```

## Seeding Database (Backend only)

```bash
cd apps/backend
bun run seed
```

## Common Mistakes to AVOID

```bash
# WRONG -- npm/npx don't exist in this project
npx tsc --noEmit
npm install
npm run dev

# CORRECT -- always use bun
bun run typecheck
bun install
bun run dev

# WRONG -- using tsc directly
tsc --noEmit
tsc -b

# CORRECT -- use the script
bun run typecheck
```

## Shell Note (Windows/PowerShell)
- Use `;` to chain commands, NOT `&&` (PowerShell doesn't support `&&` in older versions)
- Example: `git add .; git commit -m "message"`
